Good: `encoding/json` storing numbers in `any` as float64 is a real snowflake-id footgun; a string-only `id.(string)` decoder is the equally tempting OpenAPI-shaped wrong fix and the mixed-id test names the contract (number 9007199254740993 plus string `"9007199254740993"` plus small 1001). `str.split(',')` breaking `"harbor, quay"` is the usual dest-CSV trap; a quote-lookahead regex still cannot satisfy a test that requires doubled quotes `"harbor, ""quay"""`. Stale 502 fallback now compares dest want exact 9007199254740993 / two fields against a second file still on the rounded id / three-token split (r02 densification).